From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3ds-d2 <3ds-d2@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:16:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 3DS mmap: the app can lend the guest arena block
 (dyn86_ctr_arena_take)

newlib's memalign asks for size + 16 MiB at once, so a 77 MiB arena
would need 93 of the CIA's 95 MiB heap still contiguous when the backend
maps it, after Game.exe (3.6 MB) is already read. The app reserves the
block first thing and lends it through weak hooks: to cpu_box86's probe
(alignment slack 0) and then to the arena itself. Refs exsilium/3ds-d2#15.
---
 src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c b/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
index 494b374..aa9b406 100644
--- a/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
+++ b/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
@@ -170,6 +170,17 @@ static int in_jitpool(void* p)
            (uint8_t*)p < dyn86_ctr_jitpool + dyn86_ctr_jitpool_size;
 }
 
+/* An arena block the app reserved itself (16 MiB-aligned), lent for any
+ * request it can hold, or NULL (the default). newlib's memalign asks for
+ * len + 16 MiB at once (below), which an app whose arena is most of its heap
+ * only has before its startup takes a share: the game CIA reserves the block
+ * first thing. Lent, not given: cpu_box86 maps and unmaps a small probe
+ * first (its alignment slack is then 0) and then maps the arena itself, and
+ * gets the same block both times. dyn86_ctr_arena_release says whether an
+ * address is that block, which munmap then keeps for the app. */
+__attribute__((weak)) void* dyn86_ctr_arena_take(size_t len) { (void)len; return NULL; }
+__attribute__((weak)) int dyn86_ctr_arena_release(void* p) { (void)p; return 0; }
+
 void* mmap(void* addr, size_t length, int prot, int flags, int fd, off_t offset)
 {
     (void)fd; (void)offset;
@@ -190,7 +201,9 @@ void* mmap(void* addr, size_t length, int prot, int flags, int fd, off_t offset)
             return p;
     }
     if ((flags & MAP_NORESERVE) && !(prot & PROT_EXEC)) {
-        p = arena_alloc(len);
+        p = dyn86_ctr_arena_take(len);
+        if (!p)
+            p = arena_alloc(len);
         if (p) {
             memset(p, 0, len);
             return p;
@@ -222,7 +235,7 @@ int munmap(void* addr, size_t length)
     (void)length;
     if (in_jitpool(addr))
         return 0;   /* pool chunks are never reused (Box86 keeps its code chunks anyway) */
-    if (arena_free(addr))
+    if (dyn86_ctr_arena_release(addr) || arena_free(addr))
         return 0;
     // Executable chunks are never returned on hardware: their pages would go
     // back to the heap still RWX. (Box86 keeps code chunks for the process
